<title>BELGIUM: EU monetary committee seeks Italian pension reform.</title>
<headline>EU monetary committee seeks Italian pension reform.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's monetary committee on Wednesday urged the Italian government to engage in additional reforms to its pension systems, an EU source said.</p>
<p>The committee, which was reviewing Italy's economic convergence plan for monetary union, was generally encouraged by the efforts the governmment had made so far.</p>
<p>&quot;It was well received,&quot; an EU official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Asked whether the committee recommended any specific measures, the official said &quot;Yes. Structural reforms in the pension area.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
